FeatureName: Select and Move Tool

Description:
		This feature adds a Select and Move button that allows users to move any
    	shape on the canvas. When this tool is selected, users can click and hold
    	on any shape, drag it to a new position, and see it moving in real time.
    	When the mouse is released, the shape is repositioned to its new location.
    	This works for all shape types on the canvas.

Reference:
	USER STORY US4.010
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FeatureName: Keyboard Shortcuts for Tool Selection

Description:
		This feature allows users to quickly switch between different drawing tools
    	using keyboard shortcuts. Each shape button, including the Select/Move tool,
    	has an assigned shortcut key (e.g., C for Circle, R for Rectangle, S for Square,
    	T for Triangle, O for Oval, Q for Squiggle, L for Polyline, and M for Select/Move).
    	When a user presses one of these keys, the corresponding tool becomes active
    	instantly.

    	Additionally, each button displays its shortcut key in brackets beside its name
    	and shows the shortcut when hovered over, making it clear and intuitive for users
    	to learn and use the hotkeys efficiently.

Reference:
	USER STORY US4.011
